##### MF6: PRODUCT ENERGY-ANGLE DISTRIBUTIONS                     5049 1451  218
                                                                  5049 1451  219
In MF6 we store all secondary energy, angle, and energy-angle     5049 1451  220
distributions, as well as all residual and discrete + continuum   5049 1451  221
photon production cross sections for channels other than capture  5049 1451  222
(MT102) and reactions to discrete levels (MT51,etc.).             5049 1451  223
All data are generated with TALYS.                                5049 1451  224
                                                                  5049 1451  225
- MT5      : (n,anything) yields and energy-angle distributions   5049 1451  226
                                                                  5049 1451  227
MT5 contains, in this order,                                      5049 1451  228
For neutrons up to alpha particles and photons:                   5049 1451  229
- the production yields per particle for the whole energy range   5049 1451  230
- the secondary energy-angle distributions per particles which are5049 1451  231
  not represented by explicit MT numbers. On a secondary energy   5049 1451  232
  grid the relative emission spectra are given together with the  5049 1451  233
  parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular              5049 1451  234
  distributions. Inelastic scattering cross sections for discrete 5049 1451  235
  states have been broadened and added to the continuum spectra.  5049 1451  236
For each residual product:                                        5049 1451  237
- the production yields for the whole energy range.               5049 1451  238
- the recoil                                                      5049 1451  239
These distributions can be multiplied with MF3/MT5 to get         5049 1451  240
the production cross sections and (double-)differential cross     5049 1451  241
sections.                                                         5049 1451  242
                                                                  5049 1451  243
- MT16     : (n,2n) energy-angle distr. and photon production     5049 1451  244
                                                                  5049 1451  245
First, for each type of outgoing particle, the (trivial) integer  5049 1451  246
particle yields are given. Next, on a sufficiently dense incident 5049 1451  247
energy grid the secondary energy-angle distributions are          5049 1451  248
specified by means of the relative emission spectra and the       5049 1451  249
parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular distributions. 5049 1451  250
Next, the photon yield is tabulated as a function of incident     5049 1451  251
energy. For each incident energy, the photon production is given  5049 1451  252
for all discrete gamma lines present in the final nucleus. A      5049 1451  253
continuum photon distribution is added to this. We assume         5049 1451  254
isotropy for all produced gamma rays.                             5049 1451  255
                                                                  5049 1451  256
